# Copy to .env and fill in. Anything already set in your shell wins over this file.
# .env is gitignored — never commit real credentials.

# ── AI provider ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# These are the DEFAULTS the "AI settings" modal opens with. Changing them there
# applies until the server restarts; change them here to make it stick.

# claude | openai | mistral
# "openai" is any OpenAI-compatible endpoint — OpenAI, Ollama, LM Studio, vLLM,
# OpenRouter, Together, … Point AI_BASE_URL at it.
# AI_PROVIDER=claude

# Blank uses the provider default:
#   claude   https://api.anthropic.com
#   openai   https://api.openai.com/v1
#   mistral  https://api.mistral.ai/v1
# AI_BASE_URL=

# AI_API_KEY=
# AI_MODEL=
# AI_EFFORT=medium

# ── Claude (used when AI_PROVIDER=claude and the AI_* vars above are unset) ────
# Required for "Generate recommendations". Get one at console.anthropic.com.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...

# Model used to draft the post. Default: claude-opus-5
# ANTHROPIC_MODEL=claude-opus-5

# How much reasoning to spend per draft: low | medium | high | xhigh | max,
# or "off" to omit the parameter entirely. Default: medium
# Older models (Sonnet 4.5, Haiku 4.5) reject this — the server detects that
# and retries without it, so you only need "off" to skip the first attempt.
# ANTHROPIC_EFFORT=medium

# The system prompt that shapes the draft. Uncomment and edit to tweak the
# voice, structure, or rules. Double-quoted values may span lines, so paste
# prose in as-is; a literal " inside needs a backslash: \"
# Restart the server after changing it (or edit it live in the AI settings
# modal). AI_SYSTEM_PROMPT works too and wins. This is the built-in default:
# ANTHROPIC_SYSTEM_PROMPT="You help a solo developer turn real Perforce changelists into a candidate blog post.
#
# Write one section per changelist, in the order given. Ground every claim in the changelist's
# actual description and file list — never invent benchmarks, incident details, or team decisions
# that are not in the data. If a changelist description is thin, keep its section short and frame
# the key points as questions the author should answer when they write it up.
#
# The post is a draft for the developer to expand, not a finished article. Use plain, concrete
# language and avoid marketing tone."

# Easier than quoting prose in this file: keep the prompt in its own text file.
# prompts/blog-system.txt already holds the default — uncomment this and edit it.
# Ignored when the inline prompt is set. AI_SYSTEM_PROMPT_FILE works too and wins.
# Relative paths resolve from where you run npm start. A missing file is a
# startup error, not a silent fallback.
# ANTHROPIC_SYSTEM_PROMPT_FILE=./prompts/blog-system.txt

# ── Perforce ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Pre-fills the connection form. You can also just type these into the UI.
# P4PORT=ssl:perforce.company.com:1666
# P4USER=admin
# P4CLIENT=

# How many changelists to pull per refresh. Default 25, max 500.
# Each one costs two p4 calls (describe + diff for line counts), so a large
# value makes refreshes noticeably slower — raise it gradually.
# P4_CHANGELIST_LIMIT=25

# Path to the p4 binary if it isn't on PATH.
# P4_BIN=p4

# Set to 1 to log every p4 command and result to the console (ticket redacted).
# P4_DEBUG=0

# Where the last 10 generated posts are stored. Default: .history.json
# HISTORY_FILE=./.history.json

# ── Server ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Listen address. Keep HOST on localhost — the process holds a live P4 ticket.
# HOST=127.0.0.1
# PORT=4173
